# Stage 4 (`authored-tests`) failure attribution — HEAD-source control run

**Question.** The option-c Stage 4 command (`bun run test`) fails with 48 unique
tests on the coordination tree. Which of them are (a) pre-existing at
`e1c65975`, (b) introduced by our applied changes, (c) new/unclassified?

**Answer.**

| bucket | count |
|---|---|
| **(a) pre-existing at `e1c65975`** (fails on a pristine HEAD-source tree too) | **48** |
| **(b) introduced by our applied changes** (passes at HEAD, fails with our changes) | **0** |
| **(c) caused by the other in-flight edits** (passes under our change set, fails on the dirty tree) | **0** |
| **(d) new / unclassified** | **0** |

The 48 are **100 % pre-existing**. This is a *measurement*, not an inference: the
same command, pipeline and environment were run on a byte-identical HEAD-source
tree and produced the **same 48 unique names**, the same counts
(985 pass / 48 fail / 7 errors / 1033 tests across 303 files), and for every one
of the 48 an **identical assertion fingerprint** (failure kind + `error:` line +
`Expected` + `Received` + `at` location).

**The run also found one positive effect of our changes and one side effect.**
1. Our PIT-255 fix *repairs* Stage 3: on the HEAD-source tree
   `bun out/bundle/driver.js verify` fails (`rc=1`,
   `reference/swift/gen/boring/VectorCodec.swift:49:43: cannot convert value of
   type 'TiqianArray<GlyphMetrics>' to expected argument type
   '[TiqianArray<GlyphMetrics>]'`); on the dirty tree Stage 3 is `rc=0`. The
   HEAD-source tree therefore also has no `reference/swift/build/libCodec.so`.
2. Our `Compiler.hx` is **not self-contained**: it requires the in-flight
   `RustEmissionState.hx` (`state.exceptionClassRefs`). "HEAD + only our
   changes" cannot generate the Rust target at all. Details in §5.
3. A genuine, previously unattributed **semantic side effect** of our change set:
   `value_type_consumer.rs` loses its `Result<_, ValueError>` return and `?`
   propagation and becomes `-> UString` with `.unwrap()`. Isolated to our
   changes in §7. It does **not** cause any of the 48.

