## 5. Our `Compiler.hx` is coupled to an in-flight file (method-relevant finding)

The "method A" tree — HEAD + only our changed paths — **cannot be built**. With
only our 10 paths overlaid, `bun out/bundle/driver.js gen` fails immediately:

```
Error: bundle "rust", action "gen", step "generate" failed with exit code 1.
  command: haxe -cp samples -cp packages/registry/src examples/rust.hxml …
  packages/compiler/reflaxe/rust/rustcompiler/Compiler.hx:2523: characters 23-41 :
      rustcompiler.RustEmissionState has no field exceptionClassRefs
```

Our `Compiler.hx:2523` calls `state.exceptionClassRefs.set(...)`, and that field
is declared **only** by the in-flight `RustEmissionState.hx` edit
(`public final exceptionClassRefs:Map<String, Bool> = [];`, added at line 44).
Adding exactly that one file makes generation succeed (`gen2 rc=0`, all 10
trees; that tree is labelled **OURS+RES**).

So the honest statement of the change under test is: *our changes **plus** the
in-flight `RustEmissionState.hx` they require* — which is exactly the DIRTY tree.
The attribution result is unaffected: literal HEAD, the DIRTY tree, and the
OURS+RES isolation tree all fail the same 48.

